  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing \u2013 storage permission, not capacity or DB.\n\n- App `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` (E1) (E6), as `1000:1000` (E6), mounting `bind /srv/lab-data -> /data rw:true` (E6). DB `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` (E1).\n- App `/health` is `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- App logs (E3) show current health failure:\n  `health check failed` + `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-d449541af1680091'` (E3) followed by `GET /health 503` (E3).\n- That path is the bind-mount: host `/srv/lab-data/uploads` (E5) == container `/data/uploads` via (E6).\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is `owner_uid 0, owner_gid 0, mode 0755, app_uid 1000, app_user_can_write false` (E5). Parent `/srv/lab-data` is `owner 1000:1000, app_user_can_write true` (E8). So failure isolated to `uploads/` ownership/mode vs app user.\n- Disk-full ruled out for current state:\n  `/srv/lab-data: 9.0% used, 410.7 MB available, inode 0.2%` (E4) and `/: 6.8% used, 91426.7 MB available, inode 1.5%` (E7).\n  Earlier `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` at `upload` (E3) was followed in same log by `POST /upload 200 OK` + `GET /files 200 OK` + `DELETE 200 OK` (E3), and is inconsistent with (E4)(E7) now.\n- DB dependency ruled out:\n  `incidentlab-db-1 healthy, restart_count 0` (E10), logs `ready to accept connections` + only `checkpoint complete` (E11), `recent_events` only `pg_isready exec_die exit 0` with no die/restart (E9).\n\nRoot cause: host directory permissions \u2013 `uploads/` owned by root not writable by app UID 1000, causing write/probe `Permission denied`. Symptom: `503 unhealthy` and upload writes failing.\n",
